.TH "PSP action in tc" 8 "9 Nov 2026" "iproute2" "Linux"

.SH NAME
psp - PSP transport mode action
.SH SYNOPSIS
.in +8
.ti -8
.BR tc " ... " "action psp" " { "
.BI "encap assoc" " ASSOC_ID"
.RB " | " decap " } [ "
.BI mode " MODE"
.RB " ] [ "
.IR CONTROL " ] [ "
.BI index " INDEX"
.RB " ]"

.ti -8
.IR MODE " := { "
.BR transport " | " tunnel " }"

.ti -8
.IR CONTROL " := { "
.BR reclassify " | " pipe " | " drop " | " continue " | " pass " | " goto " " chain " " CHAIN_INDEX " }"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B psp
action applies PSP (PSP Security Protocol) encapsulation to packets using keys from the PSP netlink
family: Rx SPIs and their keys from rx-spi-alloc, and Tx associations from assoc-add (assoc-get,
assoc-del). The PSP device encrypts and decrypts the packets.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "encap assoc" " ASSOC_ID"
Attach the Tx association
.IR ASSOC_ID ,
created with the PSP netlink
.B assoc-add
command, to the packet. The packet must then be transmitted on the netdev of
the association's PSP device, which encrypts it: encap on that netdev's egress,
or on another netdev's egress followed by a redirect to it
.RB ( "mirred egress redirect" ).
If it reaches another device the packet is dropped. In software, encap runs on
egress only: encap on ingress is hardware offload only
.RB ( skip_sw ),
and in software the action drops the packet.
.TP
.B decap
Remove the PSP Rx state of a packet which the PSP device decrypted, so that
it can be forwarded. It takes no association. To take only the packets
corresponding to one rx-spi-alloc, match packets with the
.BR flower " keys " psp_spi ", " psp_ver " and " psp_dev .
.IP
An SPI from
.B rx-spi-alloc
is valid until the PSP device's key has been rotated twice. After that, the
device can allocate the same SPI value again, and a rule which still matches it
takes the packets of the new allocation. Delete such rules before the second
key rotation after the allocation; the PSP netlink family notifies each key
rotation
.RB ( key-rotate-ntf ).
.TP
.BI mode " MODE"
.B transport
(the default) puts the UDP and PSP headers between the packet's IP header and
its payload, and the device encrypts the payload.
.B tunnel
encrypts the whole IP packet behind new outer IPv6 or IPv4, UDP and PSP
headers: encap takes their addresses from a preceding
.B tunnel_key set
action, and decap removes them. Tunnel mode is only implemented as hardware
offload
.RB ( skip_sw );
in software, the action drops the packet.
.TP
.I CONTROL
How to continue after this action, see
.BR tc-actions (8).
The default is
.BR pipe .
.TP
.BI index " INDEX"
Use the action of index
.IR INDEX ,
to create it, or to reference an existing one.
.SH EXAMPLES
Encrypt the packets to 2001:db8::2 in transport mode, the default, with Tx
association 3, of the PSP device of eth0:

.RS
.EX
tc filter add dev eth0 egress protocol ipv6 flower dst_ip 2001:db8::2 \\
	action psp encap assoc 3
.EE
.RE

Take the transport mode packets which eth0's PSP device (ID 1) decrypted with
an SPI from rx-spi-alloc, and remove their PSP state:

.RS
.EX
tc filter add dev eth0 ingress protocol ipv6 flower \\
	psp_spi 0x80000001 psp_ver 0 psp_dev 1 \\
	action psp decap
.EE
.RE

In switchdev mode, carry the IPv4 traffic of a VF, through its representor
rep0, in a PSP tunnel between 2001:db8::1 and 2001:db8::2 with Tx
association 3, of the PSP device of the uplink eth0. Then deliver what
eth0's PSP device (ID 1) decrypted with an SPI from rx-spi-alloc to the VF,
whose MAC address is 02:00:00:00:00:01. Both rules are offloaded:

.RS
.EX
tc filter add dev rep0 ingress protocol ip flower skip_sw \\
	action tunnel_key set src_ip 2001:db8::1 dst_ip 2001:db8::2 \\
		dst_port 1000 \\
	action psp encap assoc 3 mode tunnel \\
	action mirred egress redirect dev eth0

tc filter add dev eth0 ingress protocol ipv6 flower skip_sw \\
	dst_ip 2001:db8::1 ip_proto udp dst_port 1000 \\
	psp_spi 0x80000001 psp_ver 0 psp_dev 1 \\
	action psp decap mode tunnel \\
	action vlan push_eth dst_mac 02:00:00:00:00:01 \\
		src_mac 02:00:00:00:00:fe \\
	action mirred egress redirect dev rep0
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tc (8),
.BR tc-actions (8),
.BR tc-flower (8),
.BR tc-mirred (8),
.BR tc-tunnel_key (8)
